-- title:
--   Unique p-digit expansion in a function field
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $M$ be fields with $M$ a $K$-algebra, $K$ perfect, and let $p$ be a prime with $K$ of characteristic $p$. Let $t \in M$ be transcendental over $K$, and assume that $M$ is a finite-dimensional vector space over the intermediate field $K(t) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin K {t}` generated by $t$ over $K$ inside $M$; thus $M$ is a one-variable function field over $K$ with separating-type generator candidate $t$. Assume further that $t$ is not a $p$-th power in $M$, i.e. $a^p \neq t$ for every $a \in M$. Then for every $g \in M$ there is exactly one family $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,p \to M$, that is exactly one tuple $(a_0,\dots,a_{p-1})$ of elements of $M$, such that
--   $$g = \sum_{i=0}^{p-1} a_i^{\,p}\, t^{i}.$$
--   The assertion is the existence and uniqueness statement `∃!` for the tuple of coefficients, not merely existence; equivalently, $1, t, \dots, t^{p-1}$ is a basis of $M$ over the subfield $M^p$ of $p$-th powers, the coefficient of $t^i$ being written as the $p$-th power $a_i^p$ with $a_i$ determined by injectivity of the Frobenius.
--
--   This is the classical $p$-digit expansion of an element of a one-variable function field of characteristic $p$ with respect to an element $t$ that is not a $p$-th power; it is the basic decomposition underlying the Cartier operator on differentials and the computation of Hasse derivatives. It is used here to supply the expansion asserted by [`AlgebraicCurve.pDigits_existsUnique`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.pDigits_existsUnique).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_existsUnique_pDigits_of_transcendental.lean

import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IntermediateField.Adjoin.Basic
import Mathlib.FieldTheory.Perfect

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem AlgebraicCurve.existsUnique_pDigits_of_transcendental {K M : Type*} [Field K] [Field M] [Algebra K M]
    [PerfectField K] (p : ℕ) [hp : Fact p.Prime] [CharP K p] (t : M) (htr : Transcendental K t)
    [FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({t} : Set M)) M] (htp : ∀ a : M, a ^ p ≠ t) (g : M) :
    ∃! a : Fin p → M, g = ∑ i : Fin p, a i ^ p * t ^ (i : ℕ) := by sorry
